From 46c41ce058ee82802e01b58fad68c36ca702ff70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:44:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Overview: a card's menu with Minimize, Maximize/Restore and
 Close

A window whose title bar is hidden (maximized windows on a tablet) has
no buttons left to make it smaller again. A long press on its card in
the overview (a right click, the Menu key on the selected card) brings
up the title bar's buttons as a menu over the overview: Minimize (not
for a minimized window), Maximize or Restore, Close. A tap beside the
menu (Escape) puts only the menu away; the overview stays. Minimize and
Maximize/Restore leave for the desktop, where the change is seen; Close
takes the card away as a flick up does, and the overview stays.

The rows are 44 pixels high for a finger, in the theme's menu colors.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 include/overview.h |   2 +
 src/input/cursor.c |   7 ++
 src/overview.c     | 266 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 275 insertions(+)

